Shawn Roske wrote:
> I'm avoiding spoilers for now, but can someone give me a hint why some 
> starting pets have names?  I had 2 dogs generate with names.  Current 
> Chaotic Female Ranger has a dog named Sirius.

Names can be defined in your Nethack configuration file. On Unix'es it's
in the user's home directory and called .nethackrc; have a look into the
Guidebook where you'll find information about what can be configured. In
your case you'll likely have some "default" configuration file with that
name predefined.

> On aside, even though I did read the spoiler on the floating eyes, one 
> still got me.  I was surprised that a newt showed up so fast to eat my 
> dude.

They don't *get* you; rather you ran into one. Don't do that in future
and you're fine. Read in the Guidebook about the travel and the advanced
movement commands, both help reducing the risk to run into one. You may
think about how to hit and kill these creatures by not touching them.
Then there are also some items in the game that allow for a safe melee
hit; but I don't elaborate on that since I assume you want to remain
unspoiled.

